{"lines": ["Voynich has beaten some of the best. Prescott Currier. William Friedman. Elizebeth Friedman. John Tiltman. Codebreakers from both world wars. None demonstrably deciphered it.", "In July 1897, the composer Edward Elgar slipped a note into a letter to a young woman, Dora Penny. On it, eighty-seven characters in three lines, built from twenty-four symbols, each one made of one, two or three small curves, pointing in eight directions.", "Dora Penny never read it. The note lay in a drawer for forty years, until she printed it in her memoir in 1937. In 1899, Elgar dedicated a piece in his Enigma Variations to her. The cipher is called Dorabella. Its meaning is still unknown.", "But look at what finally broke Z340. Not one expert. Three strangers, sharing tools. And in 2020, Yale put the entire Voynich manuscript online, for anyone to study.", "Rule three. Experts lose too. Share the problem."], "words": [["Voynich", 0.0, 0.44], ["has", 0.44, 0.58], ["beaten", 0.58, 0.78], ["some", 0.78, 1.12], ["of", 1.12, 1.24], ["the", 1.24, 1.34], ["best.", 1.34, 1.66], ["Prescott", 2.14, 2.42], ["Currier.", 2.42, 3.04], ["William", 3.52, 3.68], ["Friedman.", 3.68, 4.3], ["Elizebeth", 4.3, 5.36], ["Friedman.", 5.36, 5.68], ["John", 6.34, 6.56], ["Tiltman.", 6.56, 7.18], ["Codebreakers", 7.54, 8.08], ["from", 8.08, 8.56], ["both", 8.56, 8.82], ["world", 8.82, 9.08], ["wars.", 9.08, 9.52], ["None", 10.06, 10.24], ["demonstrably", 10.24, 11.08], ["deciphered", 11.08, 11.8], ["it.", 11.8, 11.94], ["In", 12.56, 12.76], ["July", 12.76, 12.9], ["1897,", 12.9, 15.0], ["the", 15.5, 15.6], ["composer", 15.6, 15.88], ["Edward", 15.88, 16.38], ["Elgar", 16.38, 16.88], ["slipped", 16.88, 17.18], ["a", 17.18, 17.42], ["note", 17.42, 17.58], ["into", 17.58, 17.9], ["a", 17.9, 18.02], ["letter", 18.02, 18.2], ["to", 18.2, 18.46], ["a", 18.46, 18.58], ["young", 18.58, 18.74], ["woman,", 18.74, 19.2], ["Dora", 19.44, 19.72], ["Penny.", 19.72, 20.02], ["On", 20.92, 21.1], ["it,", 21.1, 21.28]